her than a new leg up \u2014 AI monetization at the ad platforms is real but capex intensity is rising into 2H and the easy re-rate is done. But that is a semis/Asia view, not a CEEMEA view, and it drags the ratio for reasons the stated thesis doesn't own. Finally, entry quality: mid-range (50th percentile) entry on a ratio already -7% over 3m, against a constructive-consensus crowd, is the weakest part of the construction \u2014 consensus longs are the squeeze fuel if Hormuz reopens or the Fed surprises dovish, and the 7.0%/4.4% target/stop at a 0.50 base probability gives thin expected value from a mid-range start. Net: the direction is defensible but the thesis is doing work the instrument can't deliver and vice versa. If the desk wants this view, the cleaner expressions are a short in EM energy importers vs exporters, or a direct short of the EM tech/AI complex \u2014 both sharper than a mid-range EEM short justified by CEE fuel pass-through. Conviction 6 feels right for the AI-derating leg dressed correctly; as proposed, I'd mark it a 4-5 and want the ratio nearer 0.43+ before shorting it.",
